[51.251106, "o", "h' active_users_report.json — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cd /app && jq -e '[.[]|select(.primary_role==null)]|length' active_use…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\nAll done and verified. Summary:\r\n\r\n**Created files:**\r\n- `/app/active_users_report.json` — 346 active users (out of 500), sorted ascending by `username`, 2-space indented, with fields `user_id`, `username`, `email`, `last_login` (YYYY-MM-DD), `role_count`, `primary_role` (JSON `null` for the 50 active users with empty roles).\r\n- `/app/cmd.sh` — the exact jq command with output redirection:\r\n  ```sh\r\n  jq '[ .[] | select(.status == \"active\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | split(\"T\")[0]), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (if (.roles | length) > 0 then .roles[0] else null end)} ] | sort_by(.username)' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\r\n  ```\r\n- `/app/jq_args.yaml` — `filter` holds the complete jq filter; `args: []` (the transformation "]
[51.251116, "o", "needs no jq flags — default output is already 2-space indented, so no `--tab`/`--indent` argument is required).\r\n\r\n**Checks run:**\r\n- `sh cmd.sh` regenerates the report byte-identically (`CMD_OK`).\r\n- The documented construction `jq $(yq -r '.args[]' jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > ...` also reproduces it byte-identically (`YAML_OK`).\r\n- Assertions confirmed: 346 rows all `active`-only, all dates match `^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$`, output equals its own `sort_by(.username)`, exactly the 6 required keys, and `primary_role == null` ⟺ `role_count == 0` (50/0/0 split).\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.8-flash-next tools=9 surface=0192700a1561\r\n"]
